<title>BELGIUM: EU cereals panel to vote on GATT quotas.</title>
<headline>EU cereals panel to vote on GATT quotas.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee will vote on Thursday on the quality standards to be applied to wheat imported under the GATT minimum access agreement, an EU official said on Wednesday</p>
<p>&quot;The committee will decide standards and set dates for tenders for the import of 200,000 tonnes of soft wheat and 100,000 tonnes of durum wheat required under the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The vote was postponed until this week after a discussion at last week's meeting of the cereals experts group.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287-6830</p>
